#+TITLE: LAP loop return values lose temporary symbol identity
#+STATUS: TODO
#+PRIORITY: P2
#+TYPE: bug
#+DEPENDS:
#+BRANCH:

* Symptom and reproduction
Found 2026-10-31 while extending shipped-compiler-test.sh for SCHME.
Reproduced with a freshly built SBCL executable from f92d783a (runtime
source 2.3.81). Compile this source with VLISP-COMPILE LSM to a LAP,
then load that LAP and call either function in a NEW process:

#+begin_src lisp
(defun repeat-result (/ counter)
  (setq counter 0)
  (repeat 2 (setq counter (1+ counter))))
(defun while-result (/ counter)
  (setq counter 0)
  (while (< counter 2) (setq counter (1+ counter))))
#+end_src

Expected: 2 for each function, as with source evaluation. Actual:
unbound #:REPEAT-RESULT / #:WHILE-RESULT. Both speed=0,debug=3 and
speed=3,debug=0 exhibit the failure. The historical SCHME probe instead
returns COUNTER explicitly AFTER the loop; that form passes, including
Windows SBCL runtime 2.3.81 in a fresh process. However CCL still fails
even with COUNTER after the loop, at both qualities; the positive regression
in shipped-compiler-test.sh exposes it. Thus the removed SBCL restrictions
must not be presented as evidence that every loop result now works.

* Cause to verify
TRANSPILE.LISP introduces a GENSYM result binding for each loop;
WRITE-LAP-SOURCE prints generated code with *PRINT-CIRCLE* NIL. A
print/read round trip can split references to that uninterned symbol.
When the loop value is discarded, host optimization can hide the defect.
No compiler implementation change is included in the SCHME test extraction.

* Acceptance
Extend the existing shipped LAP regression with both loop-result forms;
prove it fails before correction, then passes on SBCL and CCL in fresh
processes, for both optimization qualities, without interpreted fallback.
